The plate spans about 400 px in the image, and I'm treating it as a side plate of roughly 20 cm, which gives about 0.05 cm per px.

The photo shows 3 bacon strips, and cooked bacon is typically about 20-25 cm long. Here each strip measures about 250 px, or roughly 12-15 cm. They look like pieces that were cut or are partly folded. Each strip is about 2.5 cm wide and thin. A normal cooked slice weighs about 8 g at around 20 cm, so these shorter strips come to about 6-7 g each. Together that is about 20 g. Because the strips are thick and dark, I'm rounding up to 22 g.

